# OWNER REVIEW
# The demonstration party in Mrs Gander's Show Home (Key 9; levels/primrose/keys/party.gd). Tonight's consultant is held
# up; Nim takes her place, in the suit. The rounds' lines are in party.gd's ROUNDS. Suggestive only: product names,
# boxes, the ladies' faces.

~ arrive
[if not primrose/in_suit] => garb
[if primrose/party_ready] => begin
Gander: You must be the consultant. You're late. Marjorie Gander. You'll have heard of me.
Gander: The men are still in my living room, and the kit cupboard's stuck. I can't demonstrate in front of husbands.
Gander: And your bag's out on the step, where you left it. Deal with it, dear.
Nim: Of course, Mrs Gander.
[narrator] Fetch for the bag, Open for the cupboard. Someone here wants to be useful.

~ begin
Gander: The men are out from under our feet. The kit's open. Shall we begin, ladies?
Ashby: Oh, I'm so excited. Are you excited?
Primm: I'm not excited. I'm here for the cause.
Fairweather: I've brought a big handbag.
set primrose/party_go

~ garb
Gander: Ladies only tonight. Ladies dressed as ladies. Off you go.

~ again
[if not primrose/in_suit] => garb
Gander: Well. Try again, then. And this time, dear, sell something.
set primrose/party_go

~ guest
Ashby: Isn't this nice? Marjorie does the nicest parties.

~ after
Primm: Three more parties. I've booked her for all three. For the cause.

~ punchline
Ashby: That was the most useful party I've ever been to.
Primm: She told us to ask our husbands. I've never asked my husband anything. I'm going to ask him something.
Fairweather: I've got a password now.
Ashby: You'll do mine on Tuesday. And Mrs Primm's on Thursday. And the church hall on Sunday, after the service.
Nim: Three more parties. Lovely.
[narrator] Every box that goes home tonight holds a dud. Every dud goes home with honest advice.
Gander [cold]: Excuse me, ladies. I need some air. In my garden. Alone.
[narrator] She sweeps out through the back door. It isn't locked any more.

~ fail
Gander [cold]: I think we'll call it a night, ladies. Our consultant's had a long day.
Ashby: She was lovely, though.
Gander: Was she.
